WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.882 --> 00:00:16.173
"I know we counted the fruit correctly," said one priest.

2
00:00:16.193 --> 00:00:18.475
"But we'll count again anyway."

3
00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:24.079
The two angry priests went outside and gasped.

4
00:00:26.922 --> 00:00:29.364
The ginseng tree was lying on the ground.

5
00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:33.479
It was gray, and all its leaves were gone.

6
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.801
tree is dead!"

7
00:00:36.081 --> 00:00:37.062
cried one priest.

8
00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:39.123
"That monkey must have done this."

9
00:00:41.225 --> 00:00:44.328
"But the monkey was inside the whole time," said the other priest.

10
00:00:45.249 --> 00:00:46.770
"How could he have been out here also?"

11
00:00:48.932 --> 00:00:50.733
a spirit," said the first priest.

12
00:00:50.753 --> 00:00:52.375
"He must have used magic."

13
00:00:54.276 --> 00:00:56.118
He looked at the tree and shook his head.

14
00:00:56.138 --> 00:00:58.620
"This tree was older than Heaven and Earth.

15
00:00:59.328 --> 00:01:01.029
The monkey must be very powerful."

16
00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:05.372
"It would be dangerous for us to fight him," said the other priest.

17
00:01:05.392 --> 00:01:10.134
"Let's wait for our master, the Great Immortal, to return."

18
00:01:12.556 --> 00:01:16.498
Inside the abbey the Tang Monk was scolding his companions.

19
00:01:16.518 --> 00:01:19.680
"We are guests here," he said.

20
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.342
"I am very upset you stole fruit from our hosts."

21
00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:26.604
The priests came back in.

22
00:01:28.768 --> 00:01:30.869
"We owe you an apology," said one.

23
00:01:30.889 --> 00:01:34.530
"None of the ginseng fruit is missing after all."

24
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:37.352
"Oh," said the Tang Monk.

25
00:01:37.372 --> 00:01:38.912
"I'm glad to hear that."

26
00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:42.674
"Thank you for your apology," said Bajie.

27
00:01:43.714 --> 00:01:46.475
Wukong gave the priests a suspicious look.

28
00:01:47.776 --> 00:01:48.976
knew they were lying.

29
00:01:49.357 --> 00:01:50.817
But he didn't know why.

30
00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:55.839
"You're all welcome to spend the night," said one of the priests.

31
00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.240
"Follow us."

32
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.861
The priests led the group to a small room in the abbey.

33
00:02:04.001 --> 00:02:06.742
The Tang Monk and his companions went inside.

34
00:02:06.762 --> 00:02:10.443
"This is a nice room," said Bajie.

35
00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:13.824
Wukong noticed that the priests didn't come in.

36
00:02:14.764 --> 00:02:18.825
He was about to say something when one priest slammed the door shut.

37
00:02:21.106 --> 00:02:22.126
A lock clicked.

38
00:02:24.987 --> 00:02:25.807
cried Bajie.

39
00:02:25.827 --> 00:02:27.787
"What kind of hosts are you?

40
00:02:28.468 --> 00:02:30.597
You locked us in!"

41
00:02:31.738 --> 00:02:32.658
He kicked the door.

42
00:02:32.678 --> 00:02:34.700
"Ow! My foot!"

43
00:02:36.181 --> 00:02:38.664
Bajie fell to the floor, rubbing his foot.

44
00:02:38.684 --> 00:02:42.107
"Why did they lock us in here?"

45
00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.228
asked the Tang Monk.

46
00:02:44.809 --> 00:02:46.831
afraid of us," said Wukong.

47
00:02:46.851 --> 00:02:49.373
"I knocked down their ginseng tree."

48
00:02:52.376 --> 00:02:53.997
"What?" cried the Tang Monk.

49
00:02:54.017 --> 00:02:57.040
"I was angry at them," said Wukong.

50
00:02:57.756 --> 00:03:01.757
"They're probably planning to keep us locked in here until their master comes back."

51
00:03:04.878 --> 00:03:06.959
The Tang Monk glared at his companions.

52
00:03:06.979 --> 00:03:11.820
"How will I ever reach the Western Paradise with companions like you?"

53
00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:12.580
he asked.

54
00:03:14.721 --> 00:03:15.181
stood up.

55
00:03:15.201 --> 00:03:16.841
"It's not my fault.

56
00:03:17.361 --> 00:03:18.122
I was hungry."

57
00:03:19.582 --> 00:03:21.082
Wujing looked at the ground.

58
00:03:22.923 --> 00:03:24.923
don't worry," said Wukong.

59
00:03:24.943 --> 00:03:27.236
"I'll get us out of here.

60
00:03:27.296 --> 00:03:30.537
When the priests go to sleep, I'll use my lock-picking magic.

61
00:03:31.398 --> 00:03:32.638
Then we'll be on our way."

62
00:03:35.539 --> 00:03:38.861
The four travelers escaped that night and headed west.

63
00:03:41.982 --> 00:03:44.383
The next day they saw an old man on the road.

64
00:03:46.404 --> 00:03:47.784
me," said the man.

65
00:03:47.804 --> 00:03:50.025
"Did you come from the abbey?"

66
00:03:51.526 --> 00:03:54.667
Tang Monk glanced nervously at his companions.

67
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.521
"Um, yes," he said.

68
00:03:58.782 --> 00:04:00.423
thought so," said the man.

69
00:04:01.644 --> 00:04:03.746
He suddenly stood much taller.

70
00:04:05.687 --> 00:04:06.988
am the Great Immortal!

71
00:04:08.249 --> 00:04:10.531
You destroyed my ginseng tree.

72
00:04:11.692 --> 00:04:15.514
You're not going any farther until you give me a new one!"

73
00:04:17.316 --> 00:04:18.877
pulled out his iron bar.

74
00:04:20.238 --> 00:04:23.868
Bajie and Wujing raised their weapons.

75
00:04:23.928 --> 00:04:27.810
The Great Immortal rose into the air and landed on a cloud.

76
00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.111
Wukong laughed.

77
00:04:31.171 --> 00:04:33.592
"You think you're special just because you can fly?

78
00:04:34.852 --> 00:04:36.013
We can do that too!"

79
00:04:37.293 --> 00:04:39.494
The Great Immortal raised an eyebrow.

80
00:04:40.995 --> 00:04:41.575
you do this?

81
00:04:42.396 --> 00:04:45.837
It's called Magic of the Cosmos in the Sleeve."

82
00:04:46.997 --> 00:04:49.018
The Great Immortal waved his arm.

83
00:04:49.738 --> 00:04:53.260
His sleeve swooped down toward Wukong and his companions.

84
00:04:54.174 --> 00:04:56.371
Instantly they were all swept up in it.
